---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import MarketModel from '../components/MarketModel';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Market Model - a_e.s_"
  description="A framework mapping all NAICS sectors into survival necessities versus personal desire."
  theme="archive"
  bodyClass="market-model-page"
>
  <main class="market-model-shell">
    <header class="market-model-hero">
      <div>
        <p class="market-model-hero__kicker">Elsewhere</p>
        <h1>Market Model</h1>
        <p class="market-model-hero__lede">
          A survival floor requires a clear distinction between what people must access to live and what belongs to
          preference, leisure, or market desire. This model maps the economy around that split.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="market-model-hero__card">
        <p class="market-model-hero__card-label">Core claim</p>
        <p>
          If a person cannot live without a market, it should not be treated like an ordinary consumer choice.
        </p>
      </aside>
    </header>

    <section class="market-model-stage">
      <MarketModel client:load />
    </section>

    <section class="market-model-notes">
      <article class="market-model-note">
        <p class="market-model-note__label">How to read it</p>
        <h2>Three bands, one question</h2>
        <p>
          The model separates the economy into directly subsidized survival markets, survival markets that are still
          market-facing, and everything else that sits in the desire lane.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="market-model-note">
        <p class="market-model-note__label">Why it matters</p>
        <h2>Not every market should carry the same burden</h2>
        <p>
          Housing, food, utilities, healthcare, and transportation are not optional categories. When they are treated
          like ordinary purchases, the survival floor breaks first.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="market-model-note">
        <p class="market-model-note__label">Use</p>
        <h2>A policy and design lens</h2>
        <p>
          This is a framework for thinking about UBI, survival infrastructure, city systems, and what should be
          collectively supported before the rest of the economy starts asking for preference signals.
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  :global(body.market-model-page[data-theme='archive']) {
    background:
      radial-gradient(44rem 26rem at 14% 0%, rgba(196, 158, 93, 0.14), transparent 72%),
      radial-gradient(34rem 22rem at 86% 8%, rgba(116, 156, 188, 0.16), transparent 74%),
      linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(247, 242, 233, 0.98), rgba(236, 228, 214, 0.98));
  }

  .market-model-shell {
    width: min(1100px, calc(100vw - 2rem));
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.2rem) 0 clamp(3rem, 6vw, 4.6rem);
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.15rem;
  }

  .market-model-hero,
  .market-model-stage,
  .market-model-note {
    border: 1px solid rgba(198, 180, 151, 0.68);
    background: rgba(250, 245, 238, 0.92);
    border-radius: 1.35rem;
    box-shadow: 0 18px 34px rgba(110, 89, 61, 0.08);
  }

  .market-model-hero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.25fr) minmax(260px, 0.68fr);
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: clamp(1.2rem, 2.5vw, 1.65rem);
    align-items: stretch;
  }

  .market-model-hero__kicker,
  .market-model-hero__card-label,
  .market-model-note__label {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: rgba(181, 136, 78, 0.94);
  }

  .market-model-hero h1,
  .market-model-note h2 {
    margin: 0.45rem 0 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display, serif);
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    line-height: 1.04;
    color: rgba(57, 42, 29, 0.98);
  }

  .market-model-hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 6vw, 4.3rem);
  }

  .market-model-note h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2.2vw, 1.6rem);
  }

  .market-model-hero__lede,
  .market-model-hero__card p,
  .market-model-note p:last-child {
    margin: 0.78rem 0 0;
    line-height: 1.72;
    color: rgba(73, 59, 47, 0.86);
  }

  .market-model-hero__card {
    padding: 1rem 1.05rem;
    border-radius: 1rem;
    background: rgba(243, 234, 220, 0.8);
    border: 1px solid rgba(198, 180, 151, 0.62);
  }

  .market-model-stage {
    padding: clamp(1.2rem, 2.8vw, 1.8rem);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .market-model-notes {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .market-model-note {
    padding: 1rem 1rem 1.1rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .market-model-hero,
    .market-model-notes {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    :global(.mm-section-grid) {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr !important;
      gap: 0.5rem 0 !important;
    }

    :global(.mm-survival-grid) {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr !important;
    }
  }
</style>
